<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toucouleur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toucouleur refers to the Futa Tooro people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal-river">Senegal River</a> valley and to the West African empire founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-hadj-umar-tall">Al-Hajj Umar Tall</a> in the mid-nineteenth century. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> note that Umar Tall's Toucouleur conquests of the 1850s and 1860s drew intellectual and ideological inspiration from the Sokoto model. The resulting state controlled much of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> region until French conquest.</p></div>
